/* =========================================================================
   mono-dropdown — a port of Basecoat's `.popover` + `[data-popover]`
   (basecoat-css@1.0.2, vega style).

   Styled by ATTRIBUTE, like Basecoat — and the attributes mirror the element's
   props one for one, so hand-written markup reads like the Lit / Vue tag:

     <mono-dropdown size="lg" color="success" placement="bottom-start">
     <div mono-dropdown mono-size="lg" mono-color="success"
          mono-placement="bottom-start" mono-side="bottom" mono-align="start">
       <span mono-activator><button>Click me</button></span>
       <div mono-panel role="dialog" aria-hidden="false">
         <div mono-body>Any HTML goes here.</div>
       </div>
     </div>

