   `:not([mono-color])` = primary, no `mono-side` = bottom, no `mono-align` =
   start). The element writes these on its ROOT — the host in the light build,
   an inner root `<div>` in the shadow one — plus the states `mono-open`,
   `mono-disabled` and `mono-fixed` (set once the element takes over positioning
   and writes inline top/left). The old classes (`.mono-dropdown.md.primary.open`)
   are still emitted as inert hooks until 2.0 but no rule here reads them.

