                                      `display: contents` and must not become a flex item
     [mono-activator]               ≡ EXTENSION (upstream's trigger is a sibling <button>;
                                      ours wraps a slotted one and stays out of layout)
     [mono-panel]                   ≡ [data-popover] (absolute z-50 min-w-full w-max
                                      overflow-x-hidden overflow-y-auto visible opacity-100
                                      scale-100 transition-all outline-hidden, and
                                      bg-popover text-popover-foreground ring-1
                                      ring-foreground/10 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-md
                                      p-4 text-sm shadow-md duration-100)
     [mono-panel][aria-hidden=true] ≡ [data-popover][aria-hidden='true'] (invisible
                                      opacity-0 scale-95 + a 2-unit translate away from
                                      the side it opens from)
     [mono-side="…"]                ≡ [data-popover][data-side='…'] (mt-1 top-full,
                                      mb-1 bottom-full, me-1 end-full, ms-1 start-full)
                                      — DEVIATION: the 1-unit margin is
                                      `--mono-dropdown-offset`, a prop (`offset`)
     [mono-align="…"]               ≡ [data-popover][data-align='…'] (start-0 / end-0 /
                                      start-1/2 -translate-x-1/2, and the top/bottom pair
                                      for the two side placements)
     [mono-body]                    ≡ EXTENSION (the panel's width floor, see below)
     [mono-size="…"]                ≡ EXTENSION (upstream ships one popover size)
     [mono-color="…"]               ≡ EXTENSION (the role tints the ring)
     [mono-disabled]                ≡ .btn disabled:opacity-50 — DEVIATION: 0.55, the
                                      pre-port value, because the activator is a
                                      consumer's own control and dimming it twice reads
                                      as broken

   THE PANEL IS PORTALED. While open, the light build moves [mono-panel] into a
   body portal; `composables/popup-portal` mirrors the root's class AND its
   `mono-*` attributes onto that portal, so `[mono-dropdown] > [mono-panel]`
   keeps matching there. Every panel rule is written as a CHILD of the root for
   exactly that reason — and because `>` also stops these rules reaching a
   `[mono-body]` that belongs to a card slotted inside the panel.

   `[mono-dropdown]` IS ALSO A PART NAME: select, tag-input, date and
   dropdown-table all call their popup panel `[mono-dropdown]`, scoped
   `[mono-<field>] > [mono-dropdown]` = (0,2,0). This root rule is (0,1,0), so it
   loses everywhere they set a property — and it deliberately sets NO paint (no
   colour, no background), only layout and custom properties, so nothing it does
   set can reach a field's panel visibly. Same contract as chip's root.

   Specificity contract (same as the pre-port class sheet): a part's RESTING rule
   is exactly one attribute strong — `:where([mono-dropdown]) > [mono-panel]` =
   (0,1,0) — so a utility class handed in through `cssClass` wins by source
   order, while the prop and state rules stay heavier.

   FLAVORS set `--mono-dropdown-{radius,ring-color,ring-width,shadow,gap,
   padding-<size>,font-<size>,min-width-<size>,max-width-<size>,offset-<size>}`;
   every fallback here is vega's value
   (`node scripts/basecoat-styles.mjs --varying "popover"`).
   ========================================================================= */
mono-dropdown {
  display: inline-block;
}
/* =========================================
   Root — layout and the palette. NOTHING here paints (see the header).
   ========================================= */
[mono-dropdown] {
  /* ── the six roles, each a public knob over a Basecoat token ───────────── */
  --_mono-dropdown-primary: var(--mono-dropdown-primary, var(--primary));
  --_mono-dropdown-secondary: var(--mono-dropdown-secondary, var(--secondary-foreground));
  --_mono-dropdown-success: var(--mono-dropdown-success, var(--success));
  --_mono-dropdown-danger: var(--mono-dropdown-danger, var(--destructive));
  --_mono-dropdown-warning: var(--mono-dropdown-warning, var(--warning));
  --_mono-dropdown-info: var(--mono-dropdown-info, var(--info));
  --_mono-dropdown-teal: var(--mono-dropdown-teal, var(--teal));
  --_mono-dropdown-purple: var(--mono-dropdown-purple, var(--purple));
  --_mono-dropdown-neutral: var(--mono-dropdown-neutral, var(--neutral));
  --_mono-dropdown-dark: var(--mono-dropdown-dark, var(--dark));
  /* the colour in play — `primary` unless a [mono-color] rule re-points it */
  --_mono-dropdown-accent: var(--mono-dropdown-accent, var(--_mono-dropdown-accent-preset, var(--_mono-dropdown-primary)));

  --_mono-dropdown-bg: var(--mono-dropdown-bg, var(--mono-dropdown-surface, var(--popover)));
  --_mono-dropdown-text: var(--mono-dropdown-text, var(--popover-foreground));
  /* `ring-1 ring-foreground/10`, with the role mixed in so `color` is visible on
     an otherwise neutral surface (EXTENSION — upstream's popover has no colour) */
  --_mono-dropdown-ring-width: var(--mono-dropdown-ring-width, var(--mono-border-width));
  /* the neutral half of the ring is its own knob: a flavor that wants
     `ring-foreground/5` sets THAT, and the role stays mixed in on top */
