   `:not([mono-color])` = primary). The element writes them on its ROOT — the
   `<body>` portal in the light build, an inner root `<div>` in the shadow one —
   along with every state below. The old classes (`.mono-modal.md.primary.open`)
   are still emitted as inert hooks until 2.0 but no rule here reads them.

   Selector map (ours ≡ upstream):
     [mono-modal]        ≡ .dialog (the <dialog> itself) — DEVIATION: a fixed
                           full-viewport wrapper, because this component predates
                           `<dialog>` support and owns its own stacking through
                           `composables/popup-stack`
     [mono-overlay]      ≡ .dialog::backdrop (bg-black/10 backdrop-blur-xs) — the
                           fill is `--mono-mode-backdrop`, a token, since a
                           pseudo-element cannot be reached from a shadow sheet
     [mono-panel-wrap]   ≡ EXTENSION (upstream centres the panel itself with
                           `fixed top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-1/2`; a flex wrap
                           centres a DRAGGED panel correctly, which that cannot)
     [mono-panel]        ≡ .dialog > * (bg-popover text-popover-foreground ring-1
                           ring-foreground/10 rounded-xl p-6 gap-6 text-sm
