/* =========================================================================
   mono-tag-input — a port of Basecoat's multi-select combobox: `.combobox-chips`
   (the field), `.combobox-chip` (+ `-remove`) and the `.combobox [data-popover]`
   list (basecoat-css@1.0.2, vega style), on the `.field` / `.label` chrome the
   ported input already carries.

   Styled by ATTRIBUTE, like Basecoat — and the attributes mirror the element's
   props one for one, so hand-written markup reads like the Lit / Vue tag:

     <mono-tag-input size="sm" color="danger" variant="filled" label="Tags">
     <div mono-tag-input mono-size="sm" mono-color="danger" mono-variant="filled">
       <label mono-label>Tags</label>
       <div mono-field>
         <div mono-chip mono-removable><span mono-chip-main><span mono-chip-content>
           <span mono-chip-label>Vue</span><button mono-chip-close>…</button></span></span></div>
         <input mono-native /> <div mono-actions><span mono-arrow>…</span></div>
       </div>
     </div>

   An absent attribute is the prop's default (`:not([mono-size])` = md,
   `:not([mono-color])` = primary, `:not([mono-variant])` = outlined). The element
   renders these attributes on its wrapper (both builds) plus the STATES
   `mono-open` / `mono-more-open`; the old classes (`.mono-tag-input.sm.open`) are
   still emitted as inert hooks until 2.0 but no rule here reads them. The tag
   chips are NOT `.mono-chip`s any more: they are Basecoat combobox chips, painted
   here (`[mono-tag-input] [mono-chip]`), and chip.css never sees them.

   Selector map (ours ≡ upstream):
     [mono-tag-input]                              ≡ .field (gap-3, as margins — see the root rule) + .combobox (position: relative)
     [mono-tag-input] > [mono-label]               ≡ .field > label / .label
     [mono-tag-input] > [mono-field]               ≡ .combobox-chips (min-h-9 gap-1.5 rounded-md border-input px-1.5 py-1.5 text-sm shadow-xs)
     [mono-field] > [mono-native]                  ≡ .combobox-chips > input[role='combobox'] (min-w-16 flex-1, borderless)
     [mono-field] [mono-chip] > [mono-chip-main]   ≡ .combobox-chip (h-5.5 gap-1 rounded-sm bg-muted px-1.5 text-xs font-medium)
     [mono-chip] [mono-chip-close]                 ≡ .combobox-chip-remove (-ms-1 opacity-50 hover:100, svg size-3.5)
     [mono-chip][mono-more]                        ≡ EXTENSION (the "+N more" counter chip, same box)
     [mono-actions] > [mono-arrow] > svg           ≡ .combobox-trigger-icon (size-4 text-muted-foreground)
     [mono-actions] > [mono-clear]                 ≡ .combobox [data-clear] (size-6, painted as .btn[data-variant='ghost'])
     [mono-actions] > [mono-scroll]                ≡ EXTENSION (the inline strip's ‹ › pager, same box)
     [mono-dropdown]                               ≡ .combobox [data-popover] + [role='listbox'] (bg-popover ring-1 rounded-md shadow-md, max-h-72 p-1 scroll)
     [mono-item]                                   ≡ .combobox [role='option'] (gap-2 rounded-sm py-1.5 ps-2 text-sm)
     [mono-item][mono-active] / :hover             ≡ [role='option'].active (bg-muted text-foreground)
     [mono-item][mono-selected]                    ≡ [role='option'][aria-selected='true'] — the --check-icon, unless the row has its own checkbox
     [mono-group]                                  ≡ .combobox [role='heading'] (px-2 py-1.5 text-xs text-muted-foreground)
     [mono-select-all]                             ≡ EXTENSION (a sticky option row over the list)
     [mono-more-panel]                             ≡ [data-popover] holding the overflow chips
     [mono-empty-row]                              ≡ [role='listbox']::before (py-6 text-center text-sm)
     [mono-message-wrap] > [mono-message]          ≡ .field > p / .field [role='alert']
     [mono-validation-state="invalid"]             ≡ .combobox-chips:has([aria-invalid=true]) + .field[data-invalid]
